           MODIFICATIONS FOR ENDF/B-VIII.0_beta-7                  325 1451
                       G. M. Hale (4/19/18)                        325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
 The representation of the outgoing-particle energy-angle distri-  325 1451
 butions for the three-body breakup reaction (n,n'd alpha) was     325 1451
 changed from the "pseudo-levels" in MT=51-81 of the previous file 325 1451
 to tabulated energy distributions for each of the three outgoing  325 1451
 particles in MF=6 for MT=32.  The sections for MT=57, the second  325 1451
 excited state of 6Li(0+,T=1) at Ex=3.562 MeV, were retained and   325 1451
 renamed MT=51, because it decays only by gamma emission.  The 3   325 1451
 other low-lying excited T=0 levels of 6Li, 3+, 2+, and 1+, res-   325 1451
 pectively, were included explicitly in the continuum spectra cal- 325 1451
 culated from a 3-body resonance model that included also contri-  325 1451
 butions from the first two resonances (3/2- and 1/2-) of 5He.     325 1451
 These calculations were fitted to measured lab spectra at En=4.8  325 1451
 and 14.1 MeV.                                                     325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
 ****************************************************************  325 1451
           MODIFICATIONS FOR ENDF/B-VIII.0_beta-4                  325 1451
                       G. M. Hale (2/7/17)                         325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
 Results from a new R-matrix analysis of the 7Li system, done up   325 1451
 to 4 MeV neutron energy, were included in this evaluation for     325 1451
 MF=3, MT=1,2,105.  The results were obtained by fitting the (n,t) 325 1451
 cross section that resulted from the 2016 GMA standards evalua-   325 1451
 tion, along with data from other reactions in the 7Li sytem.      325 1451
 The cross sections were joined at 3.8 MeV to the existing ENDF/B  325 1451
 VII.1 file, and the total cross section was re-summed to be con-  325 1451
 sistent with the partials (2+4+24+102+103+105) at all energies.   325 1451
 Covariances (MF=33), and a more detailed description will be ad-  325 1451
 ded to the file in a later version of ENDF/B-VIII.                325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
