                                                                   325 1451
                        STANDARDS COVARIANCES                      325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
 Phase 1 reviewers of the ENDF/B-VI standards cross sections have  325 1451
 expressed the concern that the uncertainties resulting from the   325 1451
 combination of R-matrix and simultaneous evaluations might have   325 1451
 led to uncertainties that are too small.  As a result, the        325 1451
 Standards Subcommittee produced (at the May, 1990 CSEWG meeting)  325 1451
 a set of expanded covariance estimates for the standard cross     325 1451
 section reactions.  These uncertainties are estimates such that   325 1451
 if a modern day experiment were performed on a given standard     325 1451
 cross section using the best techniques, approximately 2/3 of     325 1451
 the results should fall within these expanded uncertainties. The  325 1451
 expanded uncertainties for the Li-6(n,t) cross section are given  325 1451
 in the following table and are compared to values from the        325 1451
 combined output of the standards covariance analysis:             325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
    Energy Range    Estimated Uncertainty    Combined Analysis     325 1451
      (keV)              (percent)               (percent)         325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
 1.0E-08 - 0.1               0.3                     0.14          325 1451
     0.1 - 1.0               0.5                                   325 1451
     1.0 - 10.               0.7                     0.14          325 1451
     10. - 50.               0.9                                   325 1451
     50. - 90.               1.1                     0.25          325 1451
     90. - 150               1.5                                   325 1451
     150 - 450               2.0                     0.29          325 1451
     450 - 650               5.0                                   325 1451
     650 - 800               2.0                     0.36          325 1451
     800 - 1000              5.0                                   325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
 ****************************************************************  325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
                 COMMARA 2.0 covariances                           325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
The covariance data from COMMARA-2.0 were added to this file       325 1451
in July, 2011. The existing covariances for (n,t) as described     325 1451
above were left in place, but the COMMARA covariance data for      325 1451
other reactions were adopted. The following is a taken from the    325 1451
COMMARA (AFCI) 2.0 report for this material.                       325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
Covariances are supplied for several reaction channels, two strong 325 1451
channels are obtained by sophisticated method, the rest stems from 325 1451
simple estimate.                                                   325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
Elastic scattering (n+6Li scattering) and 6Li(n,t)4He reaction     325 1451
were obtained at LANL by state of the art R-matrix analysis [1]    325 1451
of the 7-Li system. This system contains data for all possible     325 1451
reactions among t+4He and n+6Li at energies extending from the     325 1451
t+4He threshold (well below the n+6-Li threshold) up to energies   325 1451
corresponding to 4 MeV incident neutrons. Also included are        325 1451
n+6Li* channels to simulate the effects of n+d+ breakup. A very    325 1451
good fit is obtained to the more than 3300 data points, with a     325 1451
chi-square per degree of freedom of 1.164.                         325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
Of particular note is the excellent fit to the t+4He scattering    325 1451
data, which have very small uncertainties. This is true in         325 1451
particular at energies near the obvious resonance structure        325 1451
in the 6-Li(n,t) reaction. These high-precision charged-particle   325 1451
elastic scattering measurements put stringent constraints on       325 1451
fitting the neutron data through the unitarity of the              325 1451
scattering matrix.                                                 325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
References:                                                        325 1451
[1] G.M. Hale, "Covariances from light-element R-matrix            325 1451
analyzes", Nuclear Data Sheets, 109, 2812 (2008).                  325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
