                                                                   325 1451
   mt=1        total cross section                                 325 1451
       below 3 mev, the values are taken from an r-matrix          325 1451
          analysis by hale, dodder, and witte (ha84) which takes   325 1451
          into account data from all reactions possible in 7li     325 1451
          up to 4 mev neutron energy. total cross section data     325 1451
          considered in this analysis were those of ha75 and sm77. 325 1451
          between 3 and 20 mev, the total was taken to be the      325 1451
          sum of mt=2,4,24,102,103, and 105, which generally       325 1451
          follows the measurements of sm82, ke79, kn77, go72,      325 1451
          and fo71.                                                325 1451
   mt=2        elastic cross section                               325 1451
       below 3 mev, the values are taken from the r-matrix         325 1451
          analysis cited for mt=1, which includes the elastic      325 1451
          measurements of sm82 and la61. above 3 mev, the curve    325 1451
          is a smooth representation of the data of kn79 and ba63  325 1451
          up to 7.5 mev, and of that of ho79 between 7.5 and 13    325 1451
          mev.  the curve passes through the average of several    325 1451
          measurements at 14 mev, and is extrapolated to 20 mev    325 1451
          using the shape of an optical model calculation.         325 1451
   mt=4        total inelastic cross section                       325 1451
       sum of mt=51 through mt=81.                                 325 1451
   mt=24       (n,2n)alpha cross section                           325 1451
       passes through the point of mather and paine (ma69) at      325 1451
       14 mev, taking into account the measurements of as63.       325 1451
   mt=51,52,54-56,58-81  (n,n')d continuum                         325 1451
       represented by continuum-level contributions in 6li,        325 1451
          binned in .5-mev intervals.  The energy-angle spectra    325 1451
          are determined by a 3-body phase-space calculation,      325 1451
          assuming isotropic center-of mass distributions.  at     325 1451
          each energy, the sum of the continuum-level              325 1451
          contributions is normalized to an assumed energy-angle   325 1451
          integrated continuum cross section which approximates    325 1451
          the difference of the nonelastic sigma and the           325 1451
          contribution from the first and second levels in 6li.    325 1451
          the steep rise of the pseudo-level cross sections from   325 1451
          their thresholds and the use of fixed bin widths over    325 1451
          finite angles produces anomolous structure in the        325 1451
          individual cross sections which is especially apparent   325 1451
          near the thresholds.  some effort has been made to       325 1451
          smooth out these effects, but they remain to some        325 1451
          extent.                                                  325 1451
   mt=53        (n,n1)d discrete level cross section               325 1451
       has p-wave penetrability energy dependence from threshold   325 1451
          to 3.2 mev.  matched at higher energies to a curve       325 1451
          through fitted legendre coefficients from experimental   325 1451
          data of sa82, ho79, sm80, ho68, ba63.                    325 1451
   mt=57        (n,n2)gamma cross section                          325 1451
       is based on the available experimental data, especially     325 1451
          that of ho79, li80, sm82, ho68.                          325 1451
          gradually to 20 mev.  smooth curve drawn through data    325 1451
          of pr69 and be75.                                        325 1451
   mt=102       (n,gamma) cross section                            325 1451
       unchanged from version v, which was based on the thermal    325 1451
          measurement of jurney (ju73) and the pendlebury          325 1451
          evaluation (pe64) at higher energies.                    325 1451
   mt=103        (n,p) cross section                               325 1451
       threshold to 9 mev, based on the data of ba65.extended to   325 1451
          20 mev through the 14 mev data of fr54 and ba53.         325 1451
   mt=105        (n,t) cross section                               325 1451
       below 3 mev, values are taken from the r-matrix analysis,   325 1451
